{
  "rules": [
    "Strong positive bias: model systematically overpredicts levels by ~5–10 EUR across most of the 30d horizon, especially after the first week.",
    "Trend/turning-point miss: model extrapolates recent strength upward while realized prices mean-revert and trend down; apply mean-reversion toward recent 30d average rather than continuing the last upswing.",
    "Overshoot after spikes: following local highs (~71–73), model projects further gains, but outcomes typically reverse sharply; cap upside and introduce a downward correction immediately after a spike.",
    "Horizon-dependent drift: forecast error grows with lead time (small early, large mid/late horizon); increase negative adjustment with horizon (e.g., progressively larger downward shift after day ~7–10).",
    "Volatility misallocation: model keeps prices in a narrow high band while reality breaks lower; allow for regime shift/downside tail risk when recent history shows weakening momentum."
  ]
}
